  "decision_conditions": [
    "The dwelling would form an incongruous feature in the street-scene and would be conspicuous through its narrower form, lower roof height and differing fenestration compared to the building it will be attached to, which fails to take into account the character of the street scene and would appear visually prominent.  The proposals would therefore be contrary to Policies 10, 7 and 26 of the Havering Local Plan 2016-2031 and also the NPPF which requires fundamentally that development add to the overall quality of the area whilst also establishing or maintaining a strong sense of place.",
    "The proposed dwelling would, by reason of its positioning, scale, bulk and proximity to the nearby boundary with the property at no.130 Victoria Road, be an intrusive, overbearing and unneighbourly development that would have a significant adverse effect on the amenities of these adjacent occupiers resulting in overlooking into their rear garden with an overbearing impact contrary to Policy 7 of the Havering Local Plan and the Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document.",
    "There would be a poor outlook from the ground floor rear habitable room windows and probable low ceiling heights resulting in a poor quality living environment for future occupiers, as well as the unpractical and problematic relocated amenity area for the adjoining flats and loss of a side access door to a flat, resulting in substandard residential accommodation to the detriment of the amenity of future occupants of this proposed dwelling and existing occupants of the adjoining dwellings.  The proposals would therefore be contrary to Policies 10, 7 and 26 of the Havering Local Plan 2016-2031 and Policy D6 of the London Plan.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, it was necessary to issue a decision as close to the statutory timeframe as possible as opposed to seeking amendments which would have significantly delayed the application.",
    "In the event that this application is allowed through the appeals process the proposals would be liable for the following CIL contributions:",
    "Mayoral CIL (MCIL2) contribution of £1750 (x £25 per sqm).",
    "Havering CIL (HCIL) contribution of £8750 (x £125 per sqm).",
    "Each contribution would be subject to indexation."
  ],
